<p>The obelix at the Little Bighorn Battlefield is not the only memorial to his service. In 1905, his mother had a plaque installed in St. John's Episcopal Church; Edinburgh, Scotland. The 8 inch high by 2 foot 5 inch long brass plaque, complete with the family's coat of arms, is mounted in the north aisle of the church and reads, "In Memory of John Stuart Stuart Forbes, 7th Regt., United States Cavalry, Born 28 May 1849. Killed in Action 25 June 1876." Click to Enlarge</p>

